l with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [144 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [145 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [157 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [171 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [190 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [191 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [211 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [212 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [257 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [374 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [500 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [556 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[49 35] [68 26] [94 12] [94 22] [106 60] [136 22] [151 50] [259 14] [259 24] [296 31] [311 14] [311 24] [313 39] [338 40] [360 26] [380 63] [410 37] [427 32] [442 31] [484 37] [532 14] [532 24] [561 40] [592 40]]} (go/file "builtins_signal.go" :imports [


